From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: carry clip/cull distances through the GS and
 ViewportIndex to the FS on v10+ biblioklept

Old CTS failures on the G615 (beta.10 to beta.17), all from code reading:

clipping.user_defined through a GS (100 cases). The GS kernel stores
only the lanes the shader writes into its records, and the GS
passthrough copies whole vec4 slots, so the clip lanes past the clip
array size kept whatever the prerast arena held. The FS kills on any
lane < 0, which made the result depend on the earlier cases (16 of
them pass alone). Cull distances stayed packed after the clip ones
(nir_merge_clip_cull_distance_vars) in CLIP_DIST0/1, so the FS clipped
per pixel on them instead of culling the primitive. A GS or TCS that
reads gl_in[].gl_CullDistance read the VS/TES clip padding, because
those records keep cull in CULL_DIST0/1.

gl_CullDistance read in the FS (28 more cases, no GS needed). The FS
got 0: CULL_DIST0/1 only carried the "cull < 0" flags.

draw.*shader_viewport_index.fragment_shader_2..16 (60 cases). A VS
that writes ViewportIndex is drawn through the vp passthrough, which
drops ViewportIndex (not a HW varying here). The FS is linked against
that layout, so its load read 0 (pan_nir_resize_varying_io).

On v10+:
- VS/TES keep the raw cull distances in CULL_DIST0/1 and write the
  flags to two spare generic slots (TEX0/TEX1). The FS kills on clip
  and flags and reads gl_CullDistance from CULL_DIST0/1.
- GS and TCS inputs and GS outputs point the cull array back at
  CULL_DIST0. A lone input array is only taken as cull if its name says
  so. GS transform feedback maps the cull lanes the same way.
- The GS passthrough sets unused clip lanes to +1 and unused cull lanes
  to 0, and writes the cull flags.
- The VS vp passthrough and the GS passthrough write a flat copy of
  ViewportIndex (TEX2), and the FS reads gl_ViewportIndex from it.
v6-v9 are unchanged.

Cost: one or two extra vec4 varyings for shaders that use cull
distances, and one int varying for VS/TES/GS ViewportIndex writers.

panvk_vX_shader.c changes are one line for one line. The helpers are
at the end of the file and in panvk_vX_clip_vp.h, so the jm-v9 hunks
that follow in the series still apply without offsets.

draw.renderpass.depth_bias.depth_bias_patch_list_tri_line is not
addressed (root cause not found).

Build-only; not device-tested.

